            }
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " is built on "
          },
          {
            "type": "glossaryTooltip",
            "attrs": {
              "termSlug": "braising"
            }
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " . cooking the peppers, onion, and tomato slowly together in a covered pan until everything softens and merges into one sweet, yielding stew. The key technique is patience: 35 to 40 minutes of low, covered cooking is what develops the flavour. This recipe serves 4."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Use a mix of red and yellow peppers for colour and a balance of sweetness. Green peppers can be added for a slightly more bitter note."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
